## 17. Lessons Learned

### Technical Lessons

- SwiftUI makes UI iteration fast, but large views can become difficult to maintain.
- State management is critical when values must carry across many steps.
- Conditional navigation should be designed early when workflows have multiple outcomes.
- Asset naming consistency prevents many UI bugs.
- AI-generated numerical output should be parsed carefully and verified.

### Design Lessons

- Beginner-friendly language is a product feature.
- Teens need reassurance and clarity, not intimidating warnings.
- Removing unnecessary visual elements can make a screen feel more focused.
- Consistent cards make repeated learning steps easier to understand.
- Small animations can guide attention when used intentionally.

### Project Management Lessons

- Frequent small commits are easier to reason about.
- Documentation should grow alongside the project.
- Reverting experiments is normal and healthy.
- GitHub sync issues should be solved with rebase or pull before pushing.

### Software Engineering Lessons

- MVPs often begin messy, but clear future refactors can control technical debt.
- User feedback through screenshots is extremely valuable.
- A working prototype can evolve significantly through iteration.
- Safety and privacy matter even in educational apps.

