## 19. Final Reflection

Tax Buddy evolved from a guided tax form app into a more thoughtful educational tool. The project demonstrates how software design changes when the target user becomes clearer. Once the app focused on teenagers and first-time filers, decisions about wording, spacing, warnings, fake data, and conditional paths became easier to make.

The biggest challenge was balancing accuracy with simplicity. Tax filing is serious, but the app needed to avoid sounding scary. The solution was to be direct, honest, and supportive: explain what the number means, show where it goes, and remind users that estimates are not professional advice.

The biggest technical challenge was managing a complex multi-step workflow inside `StepsView.swift`. The app tracks practice data, real user inputs, tax estimates, images, cards, and conditional navigation. While this worked for fast iteration, it also revealed the need for future refactoring into services and dedicated data sources.

The biggest success was the Practice Mode pivot. By using fake filer profiles, Tax Buddy became safer and more realistic. Users can learn with names, SSNs, addresses, income, withholding, and bank details without risking real personal data. That change made the project feel less like a static guide and more like a hands-on learning simulation.

Overall, Tax Buddy shows engineering growth across product thinking, UI design, SwiftUI implementation, debugging, GitHub workflow, and documentation. The final app is not just a tax helper; it is a learning experience built to make an intimidating adult task feel understandable for beginners.
